  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Branding and Communications Support for the UK Health Platform in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The British Embassy Jakarta (BEJ) is establishing a unified UK Health Platform in Indonesia to bring together UK Government health engagement across policy dialogue, technical cooperation, multilateral engagement, Official Development Assistance (ODA) through the FCDO&#x2019;s Health Community of Expertise, non-ODA activity, health innovation and growth-linked partnerships. As UK ODA to Indonesia decreases, BEJ needs a more coordinated and visible way to present this work to the Government of Indonesia, delivery partners, businesses and wider stakeholders. The platform will strengthen the UK&#x2019;s proposition, support delivery of the health commitments under the UK&#x2013;Indonesia Strategic Partnership, and position the UK as a coherent, long-term partner in Indonesia&#x2019;s health agenda. BEJ therefore seeks to procure a Jakarta-based or Indonesia-experienced branding and communications partner to develop the platform&#x2019;s visual and verbal identity, establish a professional platform presence, and prepare a time-bound communications plan to support its launch.</narrative>
  </description>
